.TH BOLT11 1 2026-10-25 "blocktools 0.2.0" "blocktools manual"
.SH NAME
bolt11 \- decode a BOLT11 Lightning invoice and (via the library) re\-encode it byte\-identically
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
bolt11 <invoice>   (or pipe the invoice on stdin)
  Decode a BOLT11 Lightning invoice: bech32 + tagged fields + the payee pubkey recovered from the
  signature; re\-encodes byte\-identically. Offline, reads only the public invoice string, holds no key.
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
.RS 2
  bolt11 <invoice>           or   printf %s "<invoice>" | bolt11
.RE
.fi
stdout: one JSON line {tool,status,network,currency,amount_msat?,amount_raw?,timestamp,payment_hash?,
description?,description_hash?,payment_secret?,payee_pubkey?,recovered_payee,expiry?,
min_final_cltv_expiry?,features?,fallback?,routing_hints,signature,recovery_id}. The payee pubkey is
RECOVERED from the signature (and `payee_pubkey` is the invoice's own `n` tag when present). The decode
and re\-encode logic lives in blocktools\-tx (`tx::bolt11`), shared with the `bolt11Decode`/`bolt11Reencode`
wasm exports so the tool and the binding cannot disagree. Offline, public input, no keys.
.SH OPTIONS
No flags. Input is read from stdin or the arguments shown in SYNOPSIS.
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
stdout: one JSON line {tool,status,network,currency,amount_msat?,amount_raw?,timestamp,payment_hash?,
description?,description_hash?,payment_secret?,payee_pubkey?,recovered_payee,expiry?,
wasm exports so the tool and the binding cannot disagree. Offline, public input, no keys.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Measured on Linux by the EXAMPLES below (scripts/gen\-man.py runs them):
.TP
2
last status bad_input
.PP
Not every tool uses the same code for bad input: some exit 1, others exit 2 (docs/FINDINGS.md D1\-14). Always read the last JSON status line. Status and failure codes: docs/REFUSALS.md.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
$ bolt11
# exit 2, last status: bad_input
.fi
.SH SECURITY NOTES
DANGEROUS: use at your own risk. Code that handles keys and signs transactions should always be read and audited by you before you trust it with real funds. Used incorrectly, it can destroy your money.
Used incorrectly (wrong address, huge fee, lost keys, wrong chain) you lose funds; verify every transaction.
Host\-side offline tool: it opens no network connection and reads public chain data; it is not in the sealed image and sealed\-run refuses it. It never prints a key; anything it prints from your own input (a matching phrase) is yours to keep private, so send stdout to a private file.
Unit tests are evidence, not a substitute for your own review. See docs/SECURITY.md.
.SH SEE ALSO
blocktools(7), docs/SECURITY.md, docs/getting\-started.md, recipes/README.md
